===Etymology=== 
From {{etyl|oc|en}} {{term|brocada|lang=oc}} and {{etyl|es|en}} and {{etyl|pt|en}} {{term|brocado|lang=es}}, influenced by French {{term|brocart|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|broccato|lang=it}}, from {{term|brocco|lang=it}}, ultimately from {{etyl|cel-gau|en}}

===Pronunciation===
* Rhymes [[Rhymes:English:-eɪd|-eɪd]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|countable|uncountable|lang=en}} A thick heavy [[fabric]] into which raised patterns have been [[woven]].
# An item decorated with brocade.

